<title>FINLAND: Baltic Ice - New ice outside northern bays.</title>
<headline>Baltic Ice - New ice outside northern bays.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ice levels were still well below average as the ice edge at the far northern end of the Gulf of Bothnia moved from bays to the open sea above 65 degrees north, the Finnish Institute of Marine Research said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Only bays had fast ice but new ice was forming off the coast, it said in its bi-weekly report.</p>
<p>Fast ice off the Finnish ports of Kemi and Oulu and off the port of Lulea in Sweden was between five and 10 centimetres thick, it said.</p>
<p>Ports further south were still completely clear, with water temperatures ranging from one to five degrees Celsius in the Gulf of Bothnia and from three to six degrees in the Gulf of Finland, the institute said.</p>
